,"text":" \n \n \nMeaning of Severely disabled person\n20","tree_line_end":555,"tree_line_start":535},{"depth":4,"role":"TD","text":" \n \n \nMeaning of Severely disabled person","tree_line_end":547,"tree_line_start":537},{"depth":5,"role":"P","text":" \n \n \nMeaning of Severely disabled person","tree_line_end":547,"tree_line_start":541},{"depth":4,"role":"TD","text":"20","tree_line_end":555,"tree_line_start":548},{"depth":5,"role":"P","text":"20","tree_line_end":555,"tree_line_start":552},{"depth":3,"role":"TR","text":"Annotations\n ","tree_line_end":573,"tree_line_start":556},{"depth":4,"role":"TD","text":"Annotations","tree_line_end":565,"tree_line_start":558},{"depth":5,"role":"P","text":"Annotations","tree_line_end":565,"tree_line_start":562},{"depth":4,"role":"TD","text":" ","tree_line_end":573,"tree_line_start":566},{"depth":5,"role":"P","text":" ","tree_line_end":573,"tree_line_start":570},{"depth":3,"role":"TR","text":"Contacts\n ","tree_line_end":591,"tree_line_start":574},{"depth":4,"role":"TD","text":"Contacts","tree_line_end":583,"tree_line_start":576},{"depth":5,"role":"P","text":"Contacts","tree_line_end":583,"tree_line_start":580},{"depth":4,"role":"TD","text":" ","tree_line_end":591,"tree_line_start":584},{"depth":5,"role":"P","text":" ","tree_line_end":591,"tree_line_start":588},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" ","tree_line_end":594,"tree_line_start":592},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" ","tree_line_end":598,"tree_line_start":595},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" ","tree_line_end":602,"tree_line_start":599},{"depth":2,"role":"H3","text":"Introduction","tree_line_end":609,"tree_line_start":603},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1. The purpose of this memo is to \ngive guidance to decision makers (DM) on The Social Security (Scotland) Act \n2018 (Disability Assistance) (Consequential Amendments) Order 2024. The amendments came into force on \n21.10.24.\n1","tree_line_end":619,"tree_line_start":610},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1 \nSS (Scot) Act 2018 (Dis Ass) (CA) Order 2024","tree_line_end":629,"tree_line_start":620},{"depth":2,"role":"H3","text":"Background","tree_line_end":636,"tree_line_start":630},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"2. This order\n1\n \nmakes changes to social security legislation to reflect the introduction by the Scottish Government \n(SG) of the Pension Age Disability Payment (PADP). This is to replace Attendance Allowance (AA) for pension age \nadults resident in Scotland.","tree_line_end":647,"tree_line_start":637},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1 \nSS (Scot) Act 2018 (Dis Ass) (CA) Order 2024","tree_line_end":656,"tree_line_start":648},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" ","tree_line_end":662,"tree_line_start":657},{"depth":2,"role":"H3","text":"Income Support and Jobseeker's Allowance","tree_line_end":668,"tree_line_start":663},{"depth":2,"role":"H4","text":"Definitions","tree_line_end":675,"tree_line_start":669},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"3. \nDMG 23071\n defines Attendance allowance for JSA(IB) and IS purposes\n1\n. From 21.10.2024 PADP\n2\n is to be \nincluded in these definitions.","tree_line_end":693,"tree_line_start":676},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1 \nJSA Regs, reg 1(3)\n; \nIS (Gen) Regs, reg 2(1)\n; 2 \nSS (Scot) Act 2018 (Dis Ass) (CA) Order 2024","tree_line_end":712,"tree_line_start":694},{"depth":2,"role":"H4","text":"Regular Carers","tree_line_end":717,"tree_line_start":713},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"4. Entitlement for individuals regularly and substantially engaged in caring for another person\n1\n will now extend to \nthose caring for someone who is in receipt of PADP\n2\n (\nDMG 20116\n).","tree_line_end":735,"tree_line_start":718},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1 \nIS (Gen) Regs, Sch IB, para 4(a)\n; \nSS CB Act 92, s 70(2\n)\n \n2 \nSS (Scot) Act 2018 (Dis Ass) (CA) Order 2024","tree_line_end":756,"tree_line_start":736},{"depth":2,"role":"H4","text":"Remunerative work exclusion","tree_line_end":761,"tree_line_start":757},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"5. From 21.10.2024, individuals regularly and substantially engaged in caring\n1\n for someone receiving PADP\n2\n will \nbe treated as not being in remunerative work\n2\n (\nDMG 20502\n and \n20252\n).","tree_line_end":788,"tree_line_start":762},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1\n IS (Gen) Regs, reg 6(4)(c)\n & \nSch IB, para 4\n; 2 \nSS (Scot) Act 2018 (Dis Ass) (CA) Order 2024\n; 3 \nJSA Regs, reg 51(3)\n(c)","tree_line_end":816,"tree_line_start":789},{"depth":2,"role":"H4","text":"Premiums and deductions","tree_line_end":823,"tree_line_start":817},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"6. From 21.10.24\n \nPADP will be included as a qualifying benefit when considering entitlement to the HPP\n1\n, DP\n2\n and \nSDP\n3\n ","tree_line_end":842,"tree_line_start":824},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1 \nIS (Gen) Regs, Sch II, para12(1)(a)(i)\n; \nJSA Regs, Sch I paras 20F\n & \n \n20H\n; \nJSA Regs, reg 1(3)\n;\n \n2\n IS(Gen)\n \nRegs, Sch II Paras 11 \n& \n12(d)(ii)\n; \nJSA Regs, Sch I paras 20G\n & \n20H\n 3 \nIS(Gen) Regs,Sch II para 13 (2)(b)\n(i)\n; \nJSA Regs, SchI para 20I","tree_line_end":908,"tree_line_start":843},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"7. From 21.10.24 PADP is added to the list of benefits when considering whether a non-dependant deduction from \nthe claimant’s housing costs is applicable\n1\n .(\nDMG 23770\n)","tree_line_end":922,"tree_line_start":909},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1 \nJSA Regs Sch II para 17(6)(b)(i\n);\n IS(Gen) Regs, \nSch II para 18(6)(b)(i)","tree_line_end":940,"tree_line_start":923},{"depth":2,"role":"H3","text":"Claims for linked benefits","tree_line_end":944,"tree_line_start":941},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"8. For the purposes of the date of claim rules, PADP is a ‘qualifying benefit’ (\nDMG 02264\n) (\nDMG 02263\n) if an award \nof PADP makes a relevant benefit either payable or payable at an increased rate\n1\n. This means the rules that, in \ncertain circumstances, allow a claim for a relevant benefit to be backdated to the date from which another benefit \nhas been awarded or made payable (\nDMG 02267-8\n, \n02269-70\n, \n02273\n and \n02277\n)\n2\n will apply where the other \nbenefit is PADP. Also, the condition in \nDMG 02270\n.4 is satisfied where a further claim for a relevant benefit is made \nwithin 3 months of the date on which it is decided that PADP is payable again as a result of the claimant leaving a \ncare home or hospital\n3\n.\n \n ","tree_line_end":1003,"tree_line_start":945},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1 \nSS (C&P) Regs, reg 6(22)\n; 2 \nregs 6(16)-(21), (30) & (33)\n; 3 \nreg 6(20)(c)(v)  \n   ","tree_line_end":1024,"tree_line_start":1004},{"depth":2,"role":"H3","text":"Revision and Supersession\n ","tree_line_end":1032,"tree_line_start":1025},{"depth":2,"role":"H4","text":"Definitions of 'Scottish disability benefit'\n ","tree_line_end":1038,"tree_line_start":1033},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"9. The definition of ‘Scottish disability benefit’ for revision and supersession purposes\n1\n has been amended so that it \nnow includes PADP. The consequences of this change are explained below.\n \n ","tree_line_end":1049,"tree_line_start":1039},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1 \nSS CS (D&A) Regs, reg 1(3)  \n   ","tree_line_end":1061,"tree_line_start":1050},{"depth":2,"role":"H4","text":"Supersession of a SPC award because of entitlement to PADP","tree_line_end":1068,"tree_line_start":1062},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"10. Where","tree_line_end":1072,"tree_line_start":1069},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1.\n an award of SPC is superseded on the ground that there has been a relevant change of circumstances \nsince the award took effect \nand\n ","tree_line_end":1082,"tree_line_start":1073},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"2. \nthe change of circumstances is that the claimant or partner has become entitled to\n ","tree_line_end":1090,"tree_line_start":1083},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"2. 1\n.\n \nthe ADP daily living component of adult disability payment at the standard or enhanced rate \nor\n ","tree_line_end":1102,"tree_line_start":1091},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"2. 2.\n \n the PADP pension age disability payment","tree_line_end":1110,"tree_line_start":1103},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" \n \n \n \n \nthe superseding decision takes effect from the beginning of the benefit week in which the first day of the new \nADP or PADP entitlement falls or, if that is not practicable, on the first day of the following benefit week\n1\n.\n ","tree_line_end":1127,"tree_line_start":1111},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1 \nSS CS (D&A) Regs, Sch IIIB, paras 2(b)(v) & (vi)  \n   ","tree_line_end":1138,"tree_line_start":1128},{"depth":2,"role":"H4","text":"Revising decisions on linked relevant benefits","tree_line_end":1145,"tree_line_start":1139},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"11. Where","tree_line_end":1149,"tree_line_start":1146},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1.\n the DM awards entitlement to a relevant benefit (\nDMG 02263\n) \nand\n \n ","tree_line_end":1164,"tree_line_start":1150},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"2\n. the claimant or a member of his family is awarded PADP for a period that includes the date from which the \nrelevant benefit has been awarded\n ","tree_line_end":1173,"tree_line_start":1165},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"the award of the relevant benefit can be revised\n1\n ","tree_line_end":1182,"tree_line_start":1174},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1 \nSS CS (D&A) Regs, reg 3(7)  \n   ","tree_line_end":1193,"tree_line_start":1183},{"depth":2,"role":"H4","text":"Superseding decisions on linked relevant benefits","tree_line_end":1200,"tree_line_start":1194},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"12. Where","tree_line_end":1204,"tree_line_start":1201},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1. \nthe claimant has been awarded a relevant benefit (\nDMG 02263\n) \nand\n ","tree_line_end":1218,"tree_line_start":1205},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"2\n. the claimant or a member of their family for benefit purposes is awarded PADP \nand\n ","tree_line_end":1226,"tree_line_start":1219},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"3.\n the first day of the award of PADP falls after the first day of the award of the relevant benefit\n \n ","tree_line_end":1235,"tree_line_start":1227},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" \n \n \n \n \n \nthe award of the relevant benefit can be superseded\n1\n, with effect from the first day of the PADP award\n2\n.\n ","tree_line_end":1254,"tree_line_start":1236},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1 \nSS CS (D&A) Regs, reg 6(2)(e)\n; 2 \nreg 7(7)(a)  \n   ","tree_line_end":1270,"tree_line_start":1255},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" ","tree_line_end":1275,"tree_line_start":1271},{"depth":2,"role":"H3","text":"State Pension Credit","tree_line_end":1282,"tree_line_start":1276},{"depth":2,"role":"H4","text":"Definitions","tree_line_end":1289,"tree_line_start":1283},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"13.\n DMG 78006\n et seq explains the meaning of terms used throughout the chapter. \n \nFor the purposes of SPC, from \n21.10.24 PADP has been added to the list of terms that are representative of the meaning of “AA”\n1\n ","tree_line_end":1305,"tree_line_start":1290},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1 \nSPC Regs, reg 1(2)","tree_line_end":1315,"tree_line_start":1306},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" ","tree_line_end":1321,"tree_line_start":1316},{"depth":2,"role":"H3","text":"Additional amounts for the Severely disabled","tree_line_end":1328,"tree_line_start":1322},{"depth":2,"role":"H4","text":"Special Groups","tree_line_end":1335,"tree_line_start":1329},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"14.\n \n \n \nDMG 78034\n et seq provides guidance on the qualifying conditions for, and rates of, the extra amount for \nsevere disability for single claimants and claimants with partners\n1\n. (For polygamous marriages\n2\n, see DMG \n78611 – \n78614\n.) From 21.10.24 PADP is added to the list of qualifying benefits when considering entitlement.","tree_line_end":1365,"tree_line_start":1336},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1 \nSPC Regs, Sch I, para 1(1)\n 2 \nSPC Regs, Sch III, para 1(9)","tree_line_end":1381,"tree_line_start":1366},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" ","tree_line_end":1385,"tree_line_start":1382},{"depth":2,"role":"H4","text":"People whose presence is ignored\n ","tree_line_end":1391,"tree_line_start":1386},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"15. \nDMG 78077\n explains that DMs can ignore the presence of persons in receipt of certain benefits when \ndetermining a claimant’s entitlement to the extra amount for severe disability\n1\n. From 21.10.24 PADP is added to the \nlist of benefits. ","tree_line_end":1406,"tree_line_start":1392},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1 \nSPC Regs, Sch I, para 2(2)(a)  \n   \n   ","tree_line_end":1421,"tree_line_start":1407},{"depth":2,"role":"H4","text":" \nDeductions for non-dependants\n ","tree_line_end":1428,"tree_line_start":1422},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"16. Where a claimant or partner is in receipt of certain benefits, no non-dependant deduction is applied\n1\n. From \n21.10.24, PADP is added to the list of those benefits. PADP is included in the list of benefits to be disregarded \nwhen calculating the gross weekly income of a non-dependant\n2\n. (\nDMG 78524\n).","tree_line_end":1447,"tree_line_start":1429},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1 \nSPC Regs, Sch II, para 14(6)(b)(ia)\n; 2 \nSch II, para 14(8)(a)","tree_line_end":1461,"tree_line_start":1448},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" ","tree_line_end":1465,"tree_line_start":1462},{"depth":2,"role":"H4","text":"Amounts disregarded from earnings\n ","tree_line_end":1474,"tree_line_start":1466},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"17. Where a claimant or partner is in receipt of certain benefits, £20 a week is disregarded from the earnings of the \nclaimant or partner\n1\n. From 21.10.24, PADP is added to the list of benefits which qualify for the £20 disregard.","tree_line_end":1483,"tree_line_start":1475},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1 \nSPC Regs, Sch VI, para 4(1)(a)(iiia) ","tree_line_end":1494,"tree_line_start":1484},{"depth":2,"role":"H3","text":"Social Fund Funeral Payments\n ","tree_line_end":1500,"tree_line_start":1495},{"depth":2,"role":"H4","text":"Deductions to an award\n ","tree_line_end":1508,"tree_line_start":1501},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"18. SFMFE \nDMG 39408\n and \nAppendix 1 to DMG Chapter 39\n gives guidance on arrears of benefit payable to the \ndeceased not being counted as assets of the deceased when considering deductions from the amount of award of \nfuneral payment. From 21.10.24 arrears of PADP payable to the deceased as at the date of death are added to the \nlist of benefits excluded from the assets of the deceased\n1\n.","tree_line_end":1529,"tree_line_start":1509},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1\n SFMFE (Gen) Regs, reg 10(1A)(gg)","tree_line_end":1539,"tree_line_start":1530},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" ","tree_line_end":1544,"tree_line_start":1540},{"depth":2,"role":"H3","text":"Employment and Support Allowance","tree_line_end":1551,"tree_line_start":1545},{"depth":2,"role":"H4","text":"Caring for another person\n ","tree_line_end":1559,"tree_line_start":1552},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"19. Claimants’ partners are treated as not being in remunerative work where they are\n \nregularly and substantially \nengaged in caring for another person\n1 \nthat is in receipt of a relevant benefit. From 21.10.24 PADP\n2\n has been \nadded to the list of relevant benefits. (\nDMG 41514\n)","tree_line_end":1582,"tree_line_start":1560},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1 \nESA Regs, reg 43(2)(c)\n; 2 \nIS (Gen) Regs, Sch IB, para 4\n; 2 \nSS (Scot) Act 2018 (Dis Ass) (CA) Order 2024","tree_line_end":1601,"tree_line_start":1583},{"depth":2,"role":"H3","text":"Carer's Allowance\n \n ","tree_line_end":1608,"tree_line_start":1602},{"depth":2,"role":"H4","text":" \nMeaning of 'Severely disabled person'","tree_line_end":1616,"tree_line_start":1609},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"20. For the purposes of entitlement to CA, DMG 60033 et seq defines a severely disabled person\n1\n as someone \neligible for certain specified benefits. Effective from 21.10.24, PADP will be included in this list of qualifying \nbenefits.","tree_line_end":1626,"tree_line_start":1617},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1 \nSS CB Act 92, s 70(2)\n; \nSS(ICA) Regs, reg 6","tree_line_end":1641,"tree_line_start":1627},{"depth":2,"role":"H4","text":"Annotations\n ","tree_line_end":1649,"tree_line_start":1642},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"The number of this memo should be annotated against the following DMG paragraphs;","tree_line_end":1655,"tree_line_start":1650},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" \n \n \n \n \n20502\n, \n20252\n, \n23071\n, \n23106\n, \n02263\n, \n02264\n, \n02267\n, \n02268\n, \n02269\n, \n \n02270\n, \n \n02273\n, \n02277\n, \n39408\n, \nAppendix 1 \nof DMG Chapter 39\n, \n41514\n, \n60033\n, \n75549\n, \n75555\n,\n 78006\n, \n78034-60\n, \n78611-14\n, \n78077\n, \n78524\n.","tree_line_end":1786,"tree_line_start":1656},{"depth":2,"role":"H4","text":"Contacts","tree_line_end":1793,"tree_line_start":1787},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"If you have any queries about this memo, contact Decision Making and Appeals (DMA) Leeds, 3\nrd\n floor South, \nzone E, Quarry House, Leeds. Existing arrangements for such referrals should be followed, \nRequesting case \nguidance from DMA Leeds for all benefits","tree_line_end":1810,"tree_line_start":1794},{"depth":2,"role":"Table","text":" \nDMA Leeds: February 2025","tree_line_end":1841,"tree_line_start":1811},{"depth":3,"role":"TR","text":" \nDMA Leeds: February 2025","tree_line_end":1841,"tree_line_start":1818},{"depth":4,"role":"TD","text":" ","tree_line_end":1830,"tree_line_start":1820},{"depth":5,"role":"P","text":" ","tree_line_end":1830,"tree_line_start":1824},{"depth":4,"role":"TD","text":"DMA Leeds: February 2025","tree_line_end":1841,"tree_line_start":1831},{"depth":5,"role":"P","text":"DMA Leeds: February 2025","tree_line_end":1841,"tree_line_start":1835},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" ","tree_line_end":1846,"tree_line_start":1842},{"de